{"author":{"id":"184022b3607ba23f7a77732840fea0e7c4ff71bfef758ea5a93c2a2127ca594f"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1791037813,"nonce":"ttuQimlprvW3Nb3+0gvB9p+AM1M=","title":"D5 Undo/redo is VS Code's (every change is a document edit)","message":"D5 Undo/redo is VS Code's (every change is a document edit); hide the app's own undo buttons there\n\nMilestone D approach: a custom text editor for `*.fumoco.json` hosting the built app in a webview. VS Code keeps owning the file -- save, dirty state, undo, git diffs, hot exit work as for any file -- and the app talks to the extension through a small message protocol instead of localStorage and file pickers.\n\n(Migrated from docs/implementation_plan.org.)","files":null}]}